# The packages the image asks for. apt adds their dependencies, which the
# lock file records. One package per line, then why it is here.
systemd-sysv            init: systemd as PID 1
udev                    device nodes and our rules
dbus                    system bus: NetworkManager, BlueZ, logind
dbus-user-session       session bus for UID 1000: PipeWire, gh0st
libpam-systemd          logind, and linger for UID 1000
kmod                    module loading
sudo                    the AppStore installs through sudo
procps                  ps, free, sysctl
iproute2                ip and ss
fdisk                   sfdisk, for the first-boot grow
e2fsprogs               fsck.ext4, without which systemd never checks / or /home
ca-certificates         TLS for apt and apps
tzdata                  time zones, Settings > Date & time
systemd-timesyncd       network time; the RTC keeps time offline
systemd-zram-generator  swap in compressed RAM
rfkill                  radio switches, Settings
network-manager         Wi-Fi and Ethernet, Settings and nmcli
wpasupplicant           Wi-Fi authentication for NetworkManager
wireless-regdb          Wi-Fi regulatory database
bluez                   Bluetooth, Settings and bluetoothctl
polkitd                 authorizes Settings' root helper
pkexec                  runs Settings' root helper
openssh-server          SSH, off until the user turns it on in Settings
gh0st-base           our configuration
gh0st-kernel         kernel, drivers and firmware, pinned together
xdg-user-dirs           ~/Music, ~/Pictures for the stock apps
pipewire-pulse          audio server; stock apps speak PulseAudio
wireplumber             PipeWire session manager; wpctl for volume
pulseaudio-utils        pactl, which Music and Recorder run
gh0st                   the shell and Settings
gh0st-term              the terminal
gh0st-m5-appstore    M5's AppStore until ours exists
camera                  stock Camera app
m5cardputerzero-files   stock Files app
m5cardputerzero-music   stock Music app
m5cardputerzero-recorder stock Recorder app
